---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test: SET locals (B-tree variables)\n; Tests SET for local variables with subscripts\n\n; Simple SET without subscripts\nSET x = 100\nOUTPUT GET x\n; Expected: 100\n\nSET x = 200\nOUTPUT GET x\n; Expected: 200\n\n; SET with single subscript\nSET items(1) = \"first\"\nSET items(2) = \"second\"\nSET items(3) = \"third\"\n\n; SET with multiple subscripts\nSET patient(123, \"name\") = \"John Doe\"\nSET patient(123, \"age\") = 45\nSET patient(123, \"active\") = TRUE\n\nSET patient(456, \"name\") = \"Jane Smith\"\nSET patient(456, \"age\") = 32\nSET patient(456, \"active\") = FALSE\n\n; Nested subscripts\nSET tree(1, 2, 3) = \"deep\"\nSET tree(1, 2, 4) = \"also deep\"\n\n; Mixed subscript types\nSET mixed(\"key\", 42, TRUE) = \"mixed types\"\n\n; Numeric subscripts\nSET arr(0) = \"zero\"\nSET arr(1) = \"one\"\nSET arr(10) = \"ten\"\nSET arr(100) = \"hundred\"\n\n; String subscripts\nSET dict(\"alpha\") = 1\nSET dict(\"beta\") = 2\nSET dict(\"gamma\") = 3\n\nOUTPUT \"SET locals test complete\"\n"
---
Option.Some(100)
Option.Some(200)
"SET locals test complete"
